#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - aarch64 long double is IEEE quad (113-bit);
# C libs hardcoding LDBL_MANT_DIG 64/53 fail to compile
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-libfirm-1.22.0-aarch64-quad-long-double
trigger_tool:           clang|gcc|make
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        "#error \"Unsupported long double format\"|LDBL_MANT_DIG == 64|LDBL_MANT_DIG == 53|LDBL_MANT_DIG == 113"
severity:               2
category:               compiler, platform, portability, libc, ohos, arm64
match_keywords:         long double, LDBL_MANT_DIG, IEEE quad, binary128, aarch64, OHOS, fltcalc, libfirm
title:                  aarch64/OHOS long double is IEEE quad (LDBL_MANT_DIG==113, 16 bytes) — hardcoded 64/53 branches hit #error

root_cause:             On aarch64 (including HarmonyOS PC), long double is
                        IEEE 754 binary128 (quad): LDBL_MANT_DIG==113,
                        sizeof(long double)==16, exponent 15 bits. C libraries
                        written for x86/ARMv7-era long double only handle
                        LDBL_MANT_DIG==64 (x87 extended, 12/16 bytes) or ==53
                        (double) and fail with a hard #error otherwise, blocking
                        compilation on aarch64.

rec_approach:           Add an LDBL_MANT_DIG==113 branch with the quad descriptor:
                        exponent 15, mantissa 112, implicit leading one
                        (float_descriptor_t { 15, 112, 0 }), guarded by
                        assert(sizeof(long double) == 16). Keep the existing
                        64/53 branches intact for other targets.

verification_cmd:       clang -o ldtest -xc - <<<'#include <stdio.h>,#include <float.h>,int main(){printf("%d %zu",LDBL_MANT_DIG,sizeof(long double));}' && ./ldtest
verification:           prints "113 16" on OHOS aarch64; after the fltcalc.c patch
                        libfirm 1.22.0 `make` compiled ir/tv/fltcalc.o and the
                        full library (exit 0), upstream unit tests passed.

affected_scope:         C libraries performing their own IEEE754 descriptor
                        construction or long-double format feature detection.

forbid_1_pattern:       undef.*LDBL_MANT_DIG|force.*long double.*double
forbid_1_reason:        Redefining the platform ABI or demoting long double changes
                        numeric semantics and can break ABI of published libraries.
forbid_1_consequence:   Wrong tarval/mode descriptors and ABI mismatch.

similar_to:             [E388]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

